Design for Assessability is a design strategy that focuses on ensuring that products are easily assessed in terms of their condition, potential for refurbishment, and value retention. By prioritizing this strategy in a refurbishment circular business model, companies can streamline the process of evaluating used products, identifying necessary repairs or upgrades, and determining the most cost-effective refurbishment options. This strategy is crucial for maximizing the efficiency and effectiveness of refurbishment operations, as it enables companies to quickly assess the feasibility of refurbishing a product and make informed decisions about the most appropriate refurbishment pathways. In practice, Design for Assessability may involve incorporating modular design elements, standardized assessment protocols, and predictive maintenance technologies to facilitate rapid and accurate product evaluations. This approach not only enhances the sustainability of refurbishment processes but also contributes to the overall viability of a circular business model by minimizing waste and maximizing the value extracted from used products.